## Generated output

Sites generated by the Forge are the customer's own work. They contain the
MIT-licensed Forge libraries (`src/forge/`) and template code; the MIT
License places no conditions on the customer's own content, design, or on
the output site beyond retaining the copyright notice above (which the
scaffold copies into each generated project as this NOTICE file).

Content rendered into generated sites is fetched from the customer's
WordPress over the REST API (an independent-work relationship) — WordPress
or plugin licensing does not attach to generated output. The Forge never
copies source assets, CSS, or markup from the source site (Proposal 098's
never-a-clone rule).

